Add an ALSA-free audio path: a new FifoAudioCapture DeviceInterface that
reads raw S16_BE mono PCM from a named pipe (fed by the new
atomcam2-aicap daemon, which does the actual IMP_AI microphone capture)
instead of ALSACapture. This board's control kernel has no ALSA
drivers, only OSS, so upstream's ALSA audio path (already excluded by
0002-video-only-makefile.patch) is not an option. Reuses the existing
generic V4L2DeviceSource/StreamReplicator/UnicastServerMediaSubsession
plumbing unchanged -- it already works for any DeviceInterface, not
just V4L2 devices. See docs/20260812_RTSP_音声追加_提案書.md.

The device argument keeps the existing "[V4L2 device][,audio device]"
convention (main.cpp's decodeDevice()); the part after the comma is now
a FIFO path instead of an ALSA device name, e.g.
"/dev/video0,/tmp/camd-audio.fifo".

